# Bilingual Git Commit Message Generation Rules (Chinese First, Detailed Body)

You are an expert developer. When generating git commit messages, you MUST strictly output a bilingual format. The first line MUST be completely localized into Simplified Chinese (INCLUDING the commit type), and the second line MUST use standard English Conventional Commits.

## 1. Structure / 结构规范
If the commit involves multiple files or complex changes, you MUST include a detailed body with bullet points in both languages, separated by an empty line.
如果提交涉及多个文件或复杂变更，必须在标题下方空一行，并使用列表分条说明具体改动（先中文列表，后英文列表）。

<中文类型>(<scope>): <中文简述>
<english_type>(<scope>): <English Subject>

- <中文变更详情 1>
- <中文变更详情 2>

- <English 1 change detailed>
- <English 2 change detailed>

## 2. Type Mapping / 类型严格映射表
You MUST translate the standard `<english_type>` into the `<中文类型>` for the first line exactly as follows:
- feat -> 新功能
- fix -> 修复
- docs -> 文档
- style -> 格式
- refactor -> 重构
- perf -> 性能
- test -> 测试
- chore -> 杂项
- build -> 构建

## 3. Core Rules / 核心规则
- No chit-chat. DIRECT OUTPUT ONLY. Only output the commit message itself when the user asked for the message text alone.
- The `<scope>` (if present) should remain exactly the same in both lines.
- ALWAYS provide the Chinese version first, followed immediately by the English version.
- **CHRONOLOGICAL & PRIORITY ORDER / 时间线与优先级**: Analyze changes from NEWEST to OLDEST modification time. Prioritize human-written or agent-modified code and config as the core of the commit message. Deprioritize or group generic runtime noise.
- **DEPRIORITIZE RUNTIME / NOISE / 降级运行时与噪声**: If the commit also includes runtime or generated noise that is intentionally tracked, still include it when appropriate, but put it at the **bottom** of each language's bullet list as **one** gloss line. Never expand noise file-by-file. Do **not** commit secrets (`.env`, `auth.json`, `bot-token.txt`, credentials).
- **CONTEXT EXTRACTION / 核心变更提取**: Extract core logic changes rather than listing file names.

## 4. Examples / 参考范例

修复(draft): 聊天框推送权跟随正在编辑的一端
fix(draft): give chat-box push rights to the side that is editing

- 任一端一改输入框立刻获得推送权，另一端立刻失去
- 电脑打字时取消平板尚未完成的写入，避免一秒后回退
- 拥有端仍每秒强制同步全文

- Editing either box claims push rights immediately; the other side loses them
- Cancel in-flight pad writes when the computer types, so the draft cannot snap back
- The owning side still force-syncs the full text once a second
